# Verification after changes

- **Tests**: while iterating, run the specs you touched
  (`yarn test __tests__/features/pan/pan.rubber-band.spec.tsx`). Before a commit
  or PR, run the full suite with `yarn test`.
- **Types**: `yarn typecheck` after changes to `src/` types, exports or
  signatures, and before a PR.
- **Lint**: run ESLint on the files you touched (`yarn eslint <files> --fix`).
  `yarn lint` lints and **auto-fixes the whole repo** — only use it when a
  repo-wide pass is intended.
- **Behaviour you can see or feel** (gestures, animations, MiniMap, stories):
  check it in the running Storybook (`yarn storybook`, port 6006), not only in
  jsdom — see `debugging.mdc`.
- **Uncommitted work you did not write**: check `git status` before branching or
  committing, and commit only the files that belong to the change.
- Fix any errors you introduced before reporting the work as complete, and say
  what you could not verify.
